# BUG-381: `xs.length` / `s.size` -- a plain (non-call) member on a builtin container or
# string that is not `.len` -- leaked into Zig ("no field named 'length' in struct
# 'array_list...'"). The one property is `.len`; everything else is a method call.
def main()
    var xs = [1, 2, 3]
    print(xs.length)
